<title>USA: KOCH lowers U.S. posted crude prices 75 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>KOCH lowers U.S. posted crude prices 75 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said Tuesday it cut the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 75 cents a barrel, effective Dec 10.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $22.75 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $20.50 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $22.75 a barrel, and Oklahoma sweet is $22.75.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
</text>
